"\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519389} {:answer/id #uuid "f927c200-f0bd-5da8-96d4-fd1b9ab95850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519406} {:answer/id #uuid "fcac43f6-9d84-52e6-bbc3-c7111b1c3113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519409}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519409} :answer-field/id #uuid "db460c81-b20d-5e16-92de-4539fa40eda4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0cf33d77-f213-525d-99fb-8b9182428af7" :question/math-academy-id "q-12244" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ when $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Writing the radical as a rational exponent, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{1/2}}={x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2\\,-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d2cd4ad0-adea-528f-a78f-3a888cbb65e5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519637}}] :activity/title "The Power Rule for Differentiation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518981}]}
